title: Proposition 45
---
order: 45
---
short_label: X.45
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: A major straight line is divided at one point only.
----
proof:

Let {AB} be a major straight line divided at {C}, so that {AC} and {CB} are incommensurable in square, and let the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB} be rational, but the rectangle {AC} by {CB} medial.

I say that {AB} is not so divided at another point.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="250" height="70" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.45 diagram" src="propX45.gif"/></noscript>
